<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  RUT_VentKiln_RecipeWiring.xml          UtinniPatches · FORGE_MECHANICS_1 F6
  ============================================================================
  RUT_VentKiln.xml's own header explains the crib and why this is a patch:
  vanilla stone-block recipes live on the RecipeDef side, via the abstract
  `MakeStoneBlocksBase` (Core/Defs/RecipeDefs/Recipes_Production.xml)
  naming TableStonecutter in its own <recipeUsers> — confirmed the ONE such
  node in the indexed ~599-mod set (`grep -c "<li>TableStonecutter</li>"`
  against the live installed Data/Core tree, this pass). Every concrete
  stone-block RecipeDef (Make_StoneBlocksAny, Make_StoneBlocksGranite, ...)
  inherits that recipeUsers list via ParentName rather than repeating it, so
  patching the one abstract node reaches all of them.

  xpath matches on CONTENT, not a hand-copied list, for the same reason
  RUT_VentForge_RecipeWiring.xml's own header gives — this also
  automatically reaches any mod-added stonecutting recipe that names
  TableStonecutter the same way, not just today's vanilla set.

  RUT_VentKiln only exists when mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards is
  active. Gate: PatchOperationFindMod on the kit's display name. ⚠️
  MayRequire on an <Operation> is INERT (MEASURED 2026-09-17 against 1.6
  source — ModContentPack.LoadPatches never reads the attribute); this
  operation's own xpath matches recipeUsers content that exists regardless
  of the gated mod, so without a real gate the appended <li> would be a
  dangling defName the moment it is not. FindMod is the only real
  per-operation gate.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>RimMandrake: Environmental Hazards Kit</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>/Defs/RecipeDef[recipeUsers/li="TableStonecutter"]/recipeUsers</xpath>
      <value>
        <li>RUT_VentKiln</li>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
